      "message": "ci: publish full-SHA-tagged image from pre-merge docker-build-check\n\nAdopt pre-merge SHA-tagged image publishing so the test-slot\ndeploy-to-image flow can resolve a verified, not-yet-merged commit to\nits CI-built image.\n\nOn same-repo PRs and workflow_dispatch, docker-build-check now logs in\nto Azure (OIDC) and ACR using the exact wiring proven in\nbuild-and-deploy.yaml, then builds and pushes\nromainecr.azurecr.io/kill-me:\u003cfull github.sha\u003e. The full commit SHA is\nused (not the short-7 form) because the deploy-to-image resolver\nresolves git_ref to the full SHA.\n\nFork PRs stay build-only: the Azure/ACR login steps and the push are\ngated on the PR head repo matching this repository, so untrusted forks\nnever touch OIDC or ACR and the existing fork-safe build is preserved.\n\nFor workflow_dispatch with a git_ref, the resolved commit SHA is used as\nthe tag so deploy-to-image can find the image for the exact requested\ncommit.\n\nMirrors the sibling pre-merge image-build pattern from tank-operator\n#1256.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
